 3. 💥 Trump eyes new Iran strikes 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Photo illustration: Sarah Grillo/Axios. Photo: Jim Watson/AFP via Getty Images

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Axios' Barak Ravid reports: After stating last week that a major new round of strikes on Iran was "quite unlikely," President Trump is still considering a joint attack with Israel, according to two sources with knowledge of the matter.

 Why it matters: The president's deliberations, which are likely to pick up when he returns from Asia later this week, show how thin the line is between the status quo and a return to all-out war in Iran. Any U.S. operation would involve Israel and could include strikes on suspected Iranian nuclear facilities such as Pickaxe Mountain. Bridges and power plants could also be targeted, as well as Iranian military and civilian leaders.

 🔎 Zoom in: Trump has been under pressure from different directions on whether to go back to full-scale war:

 Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu, who is also fighting for his political survival, is lobbying Trump to go back to war as soon as possible. Leaders of Gulf countries, who fear a devastating response from Iran, are urging Trump to resist that path and instead continue tightening the economic screws. Trump's national security team is torn, with some, like Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth, favoring bold military action. 👀 Behind the scenes: The White House has asked the Pentagon and intelligence experts how Iran would respond to each U.S. strike option — and whether any would avoid devastating retaliation against Gulf oil and gas facilities, according to the two sources.

