 4. 🌐 Trump, Xi, Putin hold historic summit 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 


 Vladimir Putin, Xi Jinping and President Trump arrive today for a trilateral meeting in Shenzhen, China. Photo: Win McNamee/Getty Images President Trump held a history-making summit in Shenzhen, China, today with his Chinese and Russian counterparts, Xi Jinping and Vladimir Putin. The trio tackled nuclear proliferation and the wars in Iran and Ukraine.

 Why it matters: Long before AI, nukes were seen as humanity's greatest existential threat — and Trump contends the planet's three largest nuclear powers are best positioned to ease the menace. "We are really making history," Trump said at the summit in the Chinese city of Shenzhen.

 Yes, but: No major breakthroughs were immediately announced that would take today's meeting beyond a lavish photo op . Trump, Xi and Putin met for 80 minutes in their nations' first three-way summit. Chinese state broadcaster CCTV said Xi told his counterparts nuclear weapons should be prohibited and destroyed, AP reports. 

 "We hold joint responsibility for maintaining international peace," Putin said. The New York Times reports that Trump called Putin a " friend ." Trump also met separately with Xi, the rivals' third substantial face-to-face meeting this year. Get the latest .

 
 
