 5. 💡 Putting cyber risk in perspective 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Allie Carl/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Axios chief technology officer Dan Cox, who has spent 25 years at some of the world's biggest tech companies, gives his personal view of the recent spate of high-profile system failures : 

 My parents, my siblings and plenty of other people are asking the same question: How worried should we be?

 I've been in technology a long time. I take threats like this seriously , but I'm not in panic mode. Zoom out: The way I think about it, we've put powerful tools in more hands, and people are taking potshots to see what they can hit. Those shots can do real damage, and we need to protect ourselves.

 But hearing gunfire doesn't, by itself, mean an army is coming over the hill. We need to understand who's firing, what they can actually do and whether the threat is changing. Zoom in: Over the past few weeks, we've identified bad actors snooping around our own website. Our talented engineers have investigated threats and put mitigations in place.

 There may still be attempts on our site. But each incident gives us an opportunity to strengthen our systems. 🧑‍💻 Between the lines: Thousands of smart, resourceful and dedicated engineers are working to protect the systems we all rely on. I see that commitment in our own team. If the threat grows, more people with those skills will step up.

