 6. 🇮🇱 Israel&#x27;s GOP firewall 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Photo illustration: Aïda Amer/Axios. Photos: Getty Images

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Republican voters in four early 2028 primary states have favorable views of Israel by wide margins and have negative opinions of three leading right-wing critics of the Jewish state, Axios' Marc Caputo writes from a new poll by a national GOP consulting firm. 

 Why it matters: The poll challenges the notion that Republican opinion toward Israel is fracturing significantly, and points to a potential disconnect between GOP voters' attitudes and the sentiments of those who often draw the most attention online. The survey, conducted by OnMessage Inc . for the Combat Antisemitism Movement's political arm, essentially provides a roadmap for pro-Israel Republicans' messaging ahead of the 2028 presidential campaign.

 🔭 Zoom in: After the midterms, Vice President Vance called on the U.S. and the GOP to "change our relationship to Israel," elevating the nations' longtime partnership as a 2028 campaign issue.

 Israel is supported by 68% of Republican voters in Iowa, New Hampshire, Nevada and South Carolina, according to the survey, a result similar to findings by Gallup and Pew . More on the poll . 

 
 
