 7. 📊 World&#x27;s Muslims to outnumber Christians within a decade 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Pew Research . Chart: Erin Davis/Axios Islam is expected to surpass Christianity as the world's largest religion by 2035, Axios' Josephine Walker writes from new Pew projections . 

 The shift largely reflects differences in birth rates. Both religions are expected to grow globally. Between 2020 and 2070, births are projected to outnumber deaths by 1.6 billion among Muslims and 792 million among Christians. ⛪ Between the lines: The U.S. is expected to lose more Christians than any other country by 2070.

 In 2020, the U.S. had the world's largest Christian population at 217 million. By 2070, that number is expected to drop to 174 million. Share this story . 

 
 
